{\large\bfseries\color{CoverCream} 關於本書}\qquad{\baskervillefont\itshape\large\color{CoverGoldBright} About This Book}

\vspace{0.45cm}

\begin{minipage}{5in}
\small\color{CoverCream}
$if(backcover)$
$backcover$
$else$
本書逐章研讀提多書全書三章，並附參考資料附錄，整合黃長老查經教導、John MacArthur 逐節解經、G. Campbell Morgan《Living Messages of the Books of the Bible》屬靈組織分析，貫穿全書「把沒有辦完的事辦整齊」的任務主線：第一章設立長老、駁倒假教師；第二章教導老年人、老年婦人、少年婦人、少年人、僕人五種身分如何活出純正的教訓；第三章以新約最凝練的救恩總論之一（3:4-7）收筆，指明善行是恩典所結的果子，不是換取恩典的代價。全書見證保羅如何差派提多，以任務導向、雷厲風行的方式，在一個民風散漫的宣教工場上建立起經得起考驗的教會秩序。

{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream}\lettrine[lines=3,findent=2pt,nindent=2pt]{\color{CoverGoldBright}A}{}\,chapter-by-chapter study of all three chapters of Titus, with a references appendix, integrating Elder Wong's Bible teaching, John MacArthur's verse-by-verse exposition, and G. Campbell Morgan's spiritual analysis in \textit{Living Messages of the Books of the Bible}. The study traces the letter's task-driven throughline — "putting what remains into order": appointing elders and silencing false teachers (ch. 1); teaching five stations of life to embody sound doctrine (ch. 2); and closing on one of the New Testament's most concentrated summaries of the gospel (3:4-7), where good works are shown to be the fruit of grace, never its price. The whole book witnesses how Paul commissioned Titus — briskly, urgently, task by task — to build a durable church order on a difficult mission field.}
$endif$
\end{minipage}

\vspace{0.45cm}

